# AE-19d — DND-484, end of drain when the owner already resumed: the admiral
# has released the run (fleet-resume drained), so it owns nothing. It ends its
# turn and sends NO hand-back to the top-level session; that session's resume
# waiter, armed when this admiral completes, sees the resume on its first poll.
# DND-443's step-5 re-check + `SendMessage main` hand-back is removed.
invariant = after release: end-turn, no hand-back message, no spawn
home      = athena:fleet-drain (drain protocol step 5)
mode      = next-action
expect_action = end-turn
forbid_action = sendmessage.main
forbid_action = agent.spawn-captain
